--- b8 medium.en: Medigap also leaves some things out. It generally does not cover long-term care, like non-skilled care in a nursing home, vision or dental care, hearing aids, glasses, or private duty nursing. Medigap plans sold after 2005 do not include prescription drugs, so for drugs, you need a separate Part D plan. And one policy covers only one person, so spouses each need their own.
