--- b10 medium.en: There is a second price trap. How the company sets the price. Medicare describes three ways. Community rated generally means the same premium for everyone, whatever their age. Issue age rated means your price depends on your age when you buy and does not rise because you get older. Attained age rated means your price rises as you age. In Medicare's own example, which it says is not an actual price, $120 at $65 becomes $126 at $66.
