--- b11 medium.en: Now, the most important rule, the Medigap Open Enrollment Period. It lasts six months, and it starts the first month you have Part B and you are 65 or older. It is a one-time period, and it does not repeat every year. During it, a company cannot refuse to sell you any policy it offers, cannot use medical underwriting, and cannot charge you more because of your health problems.
