--- b12 medium.en: Outside that window, the rules change. Medicare says you may pay more, you may have fewer plans to choose from, and there is no guarantee that a company will sell you a policy if you do not meet its medical underwriting rules. This matters for Carol. If her Part B starts the month she turns 65, her six months start then, and Medicare says they cannot be changed or repeated.
