--- b14 medium.en: But, there are situations where Ben is protected. Medicare calls them Guaranteed Issue Rights. One example is when his Advantage Plan leaves Medicare or stops giving care in his area, or when he moves out of its service area. Then, the company must sell him a policy, must cover his pre-existing conditions, and cannot charge him more for his health. He must apply no more than 63 days after his advantage coverage ends. His state may give him even more rights.
